# Brainstorming — Search Bookmark Integration (Search Discover · Bookmark tab)

**Date:** 2026-07-07
**For:** Frontend (pages-new)
**Backend task:** [`panorra-api-go#450`](https://github.com/GoThruMedia/panorra-api-go/issues/450) — *Update API Search Bookmark · "New flow: bookmark publish from search pages"*
**UI design task:** [`panorra-pwa#3107`](https://github.com/GoThruMedia/panorra-pwa/issues/3107) — *Create Search Discover Layout* (Feed-First Search Sidebar)
**Scope:** Wire the **Bookmark tab** of the Search/Discover page in `pages-new` to the updated Search Bookmark API.

> This is the *why/how* companion for integrating `#450` into the `#3107` layout. Read `#3107` for the visual design; this doc covers data flow, decisions, and open questions.

---

## 1. The problem / context

The new **Search Discover** page (`#3107`) is a *Feed-First Search Sidebar*: a search bar (`Search posts, bookmarks, users, hashtags…`) over four tabs — **Post · Bookmark · User · Hashtag** — with category filters (All / Leisure / Real Estate / Business), a scrollable results sidebar on the left, and the map on the right. It's useful **before** typing (shows recent content) and is entered from the navbar Search icon or "View More" in Discover.

`#450` is the backend enhancement for the **Bookmark tab** of this page — *"bookmark publish from search pages."* So the FE work here is: **make the Bookmark tab of Search Discover real**, driven by the updated Search Bookmark API, instead of the current static data.

**Current state (pages-new):**
- `explore/` renders `ExploreBookmarkComponent` / `ExplorePlaceComponent` / `ExploreUserComponent` from **static mock** (`explore.data.ts` → `EXPLORE_BOOKMARKS`, …). No search, no API.
- A real bookmark search already exists elsewhere: `settings/bookmark/bookmark.service.ts` → `searchBookmark(name, page)` → `GET /search/folder-bookmark?name=&page=&limit=12` (searches **bookmark folders** by name). Broadcast/"publish" of a bookmark is modelled via `sharedPostData` / `sharedDataSubject` → `detail-boardcast`.

**Goal:** the Bookmark tab lists bookmarks (default: recent, useful-before-typing), filters by the search query + category, and supports the "publish" flow that `#450` introduces.

---

## 2. ⚠️ Open question to confirm against `#450` (blocking assumption)

`#450`'s body is one line, so the precise meaning of **"bookmark publish"** must be confirmed from the API doc/BE before coding. Working assumption for this brainstorm:

> **Assumption:** the Bookmark tab shows **published/broadcast bookmarks** (a bookmark that a creator has *published* so others can discover it), searchable by query + category from the Search page. `#450` updates the Search Bookmark endpoint to return these "published bookmark" items (and the fields the tab needs).

Alternatives it *could* mean (confirm which):
- **(a)** Search the current user's **own bookmark folders** from the search page (extends `search/folder-bookmark`), and "publish" = an action to broadcast a folder.
- **(b)** Discover **publicly published** bookmarks from all creators (the assumption above).
- **(c)** The search result rows just gain a **publish/bookmark-state** flag to render.

Everything below is written to the assumption but flags where the answer changes the work.

---

## 3. Search Discover architecture (from `#3107`)

```
SearchDiscover page (pages-new)
├── Search bar (query signal, debounced)
├── Tabs: Post | Bookmark | User | Hashtag   (active tab signal)
├── Category filter: All | Leisure | Real Estate | Business
├── Results sidebar (scroll):  @for over the active tab's results
│     Post → post cards · Bookmark → bookmark cards · User → user cards · Hashtag → hashtag rows
└── Map panel (right): markers for results with coordinates
Behaviors:
- Opens with recent content (no query) — "useful before typing".
- Default tab = Post from navbar; "View More" from Discover opens with the matching tab.
- Search bar + tabs + filters stay reachable while the list scrolls.
```

This integration owns the **Bookmark tab** slice of that: its data source, mapping, empty/loading/error states, and any "publish" affordance.

---

## 4. Data flow (target — Bookmark tab)

```
User opens Search (or picks Bookmark tab)
  → SearchFacade.searchBookmarks(query='', category='all', page=1)
      GET <Search Bookmark endpoint from #450>?q=&category=&page=&limit=
  → runDecryption(res) → mapApiBookmarkToCard(item) → bookmarks() signal
  → @for renders bookmark cards (+ map markers if geo)
Typing in search bar (debounced ~400–600ms) → re-query with q
Changing category chip → re-query with category
Scroll to bottom → next page appended (infinite scroll)
"Publish" affordance on a card (if in scope) → SearchFacade.publishBookmark(...) → toast + state update
```

Reuse the established pages-new idiom: **facade/service for I/O · `runDecryption` · mapper → view model · signals · OnPush · no `any` · no `BehaviorSubject`.**

---

## 5. Approaches (pick one)

### 5.1 Where the Bookmark tab lives
- **A — New `search/` feature in pages-new (recommended):** build the Search Discover page as its own feature (`pages-new/search/`) with a `search.facade.ts` exposing per-tab queries; the Bookmark tab is one child. Cleanest home for `#3107`; `explore/` is retired/folded in. *Why:* `#3107` describes a full page, not a tweak to `explore`.
- **B — Extend `explore/`:** wire the existing `ExploreBookmarkComponent` to the API in place. Smaller diff, but `explore` is static-mock and doesn't match the `#3107` tabbed layout — likely a dead-end.

### 5.2 Search trigger
- **A — Debounced live search (recommended):** matches "useful before typing" + smooth typing. `settings/bookmark/input-search` already debounces 600ms — reuse that pattern.
- **B — Submit-on-enter:** simpler, but the Feed-First design wants responsiveness.

### 5.3 "Bookmark publish" affordance
- **Confirm from `#450` first.** If the tab is *browsing published bookmarks*, there may be **no publish action here** (publishing happens elsewhere; the tab just *shows* published bookmarks). If the tab is *my folders*, a **Publish/Broadcast** action per row is needed (reuse `sharedPostData` → `detail-boardcast`). → **decision gated on §2.**

---

## 6. Proposed file structure (pages-new)

```
src/app/pages-new/search/                     (new — the #3107 page)
├── search.component.ts/html/scss             orchestrator: query + tab + category signals
├── search.facade.ts                          per-tab queries (posts/bookmarks/users/hashtags)
├── search-bookmark.api.model.ts              raw #450 response types
├── search-bookmark.mapper.ts                 API → BookmarkCard view model (pure, testable)
├── bookmark-tab/bookmark-tab.component.ts    the Bookmark tab list (this task's focus)
└── (post-tab / user-tab / hashtag-tab …)     siblings (separate tasks)
```

- `search.facade.searchBookmarks(query, category, page)` → the `#450` endpoint (confirm path/params).
- `search-bookmark.mapper.ts` is the **contract seam** — unit-test it (pure function) even though the rest is manual/build-verified.

---

## 7. States & UX (Bookmark tab)

| State | Behaviour |
|-------|-----------|
| Default (no query) | Recent published bookmarks — the page is useful before typing. |
| Typing | Debounced re-query; loading shimmer on the list, header/tabs stay put. |
| Category chip | Re-query with the selected category; `All` clears it. |
| Empty | "No bookmarks found" empty state (query-aware copy). |
| Infinite scroll | Append next page; no duplicates; stop at end. |
| Map | Bookmarks with coordinates drop markers; selecting syncs (if in `#3107` scope). |
| Error | Clear message + retry; no stuck spinner. |
| Publish (if in scope) | Per-card action → API → success toast + optimistic state. |

---

## 8. Risks & mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|
| **"bookmark publish" meaning unresolved** (§2) | Confirm endpoint + semantics from `#450` API doc before building the publish affordance; the list-render work can proceed on the assumption, isolated in the mapper. |
| Response envelope unknown | Keep decryption + one mapper; verify keys against live `#450` response (like the Places integration did). |
| Building on static `explore` | Prefer a new `search/` feature (§5.1-A); don't entrench mock. |
| Map ↔ list coupling scope creep | Treat map-marker sync as `#3107`-owned; this task focuses on the Bookmark list + data. |

---

## 9. Success criteria

- Bookmark tab of Search Discover renders **real** data from the `#450` Search Bookmark API (no `EXPLORE_BOOKMARKS` mock).
- Useful-before-typing: recent bookmarks show on open; debounced query + category filter re-query correctly.
- Loading / empty / error / infinite-scroll all handled; matches `#3107` layout.
- Facade + mapper + signals + OnPush; no `any`, no `BehaviorSubject`.
- "Publish" flow implemented **iff** `#450` scopes it (per §2), reusing the existing broadcast/`sharedPostData` mechanism.

---

## 10. Next step

Confirm §2 against the `#450` API doc (endpoint path, query params `q`/`category`/`page`, response shape, and what "publish" is). Then draft the implementation plan for `pages-new/search/` Bookmark tab (facade `searchBookmarks` + mapper + tab component + states), with the mapper unit-tested and the rest build/manual-verified.

